module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Away.Basic
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.UniversalProperty
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.GradedDivide

/-!
# The existence half of the universal property of blowing up

Stacks tag 0806 says that the blowup `b : X' ⟶ X` of a closed subscheme `Z ⊆ X` is a final
object of the category `C` of schemes `Y ⟶ X` on which the inverse image of `Z` is an effective
Cartier divisor. Its uniqueness half is
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/UniversalProperty.lean`; this file is about the
existence half, which the source proves by exhibiting, for `f : Y ⟶ X` in `C` with
`D = f^{-1}(Z)`, the graded map `ψ : ⨁ f^*ℐ^d ⟶ ⨁ ℐ_D^d` of `𝒪_Y`-algebras and feeding
`(1, f, ψ)` to the universal property of relative `Proj` (Constructions, Section 01NS).

The global blowup morphism is still unavailable: it is the relative `Proj` of the Rees algebra
`⨁_{n ≥ 0} ℐⁿ` (tag 01OG, whose sheaf-level input is
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/ReesAlgebraSheaf.lean`), and the relative `Proj` of a
situation (tag 01NQ) is only available conditionally on tag 01NO, which is the hypothesis
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.ChartsCartesian` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjSituation/SituationData.lean`. What *is* available
unconditionally is the blowup of an **affine** scheme, `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec I = Proj` of the
Rees algebra of an ideal `I ⊆ R` (`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/Basic.lean`). This file
constructs the existence half of tag 0806 for that affine blowup, and reduces the existence half
over an affine base to a statement local on the source.

Over an affine base the datum `ψ` is a ring map. Let `φ : R ⟶ Γ(X, ⊤)` present a scheme `X` over
`Spec R`, and suppose the inverse image `I · Γ(X, ⊤)` of the centre is the principal ideal
generated by a nonzerodivisor `t`. Then every element `x ∈ Iⁿ` is `tⁿ c` for a unique `c`, and
`x ↦ c` is a ring map `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide` out of the Rees algebra `reesAlgebra I` — the
degree-wise form of `ψ`, since in this situation `ℐ_D^{⊗ n} = ℐ_D^n = tⁿ 𝒪_X`. Its image of the
irrelevant ideal is the unit ideal, so `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.fromOfGlobalSections` turns it
into the classifying morphism `Stacks.Blowup.toBlowUpSpec : X ⟶ blowUpSpec I` over `Spec R`.

Existence is then local on the source, by the uniqueness half: two morphisms into a separated
`S`-scheme which is an isomorphism over `V` agree once the inverse image of `V` is
scheme-theoretically dense, so morphisms defined on an open cover glue. Hence the existence half
of tag 0806 over an affine base follows from tag 02OS part 1, tag 07ZU, and the purely local
statement that the inverse image of the centre is generated by one nonzerodivisor.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Blowup.reesEval`: the ring map `R[X] ⟶ B[1/b]` carrying coefficients along
  `φ : R ⟶ B` and sending `X` to `1/b`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivisible`: the `R`-subalgebra of `R[X]` of polynomials whose value at
  `1/b` already lies in `B`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide`: the ring map `reesAlgebra I ⟶ B` sending a homogeneous element of
  degree `n`, i.e. an `x ∈ Iⁿ`, to the unique `c ∈ B` with `φ x = bⁿ c`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOne`: the degree-one element `monomial 1 x` of `reesAlgebra I`, for
  `x ∈ I`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.toBlowUpSpec`: the classifying morphism `X ⟶ blowUpSpec I`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.specHomRingHom`: the ring map `R ⟶ Γ(X, ⊤)` underlying a morphism
  `X ⟶ Spec R`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.reesAlgebra_le_reesDivisible`: if `I` becomes the principal ideal `(b)` in `B`,
  every element of `reesAlgebra I` is divisible, because the Rees algebra is generated in
  degree one.
* `Stacks.Blowup.pow_mul_reesDivide_monomial`, `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide_algebraMap`: the
  characterizing properties of `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.reesHom_ext`: ring maps out of `reesAlgebra I` are determined in degrees zero
  and one.
* `Stacks.Blowup.eq_reesDivide`: `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide` is the only ring map out of
  `reesAlgebra I` extending `φ` and dividing the degree-one elements by `b`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.map_reesDivide_irrelevant_eq_top`: the image of the irrelevant ideal is the
  unit ideal, which is the hypothesis of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.fromOfGlobalSections`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.toBlowUpSpec_toSpec`: the classifying morphism is a morphism over `Spec R`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_hom_toSpec`: **the existence half of tag 0806 over an affine base, for a
  globally principal inverse image of the centre.**
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_hom_toSpec_span_singleton`: the same for a principal centre `(a)`, where
  the hypothesis becomes that the image of `a` is a nonzerodivisor. This is the existence half of
  the universal property behind tag 0807 in the affine case.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_hom_of_isOpenCover`: existence of a morphism over `S` into a separated
  `S`-scheme which is an isomorphism over `V` is local on the source, when the inverse image of
  `V` is scheme-theoretically dense.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_hom_toSpec_of_isOpenCover`: the existence half of tag 0806 over an
  affine base from local data, i.e. from tag 02OS part 1, tag 07ZU and local principality.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide` is built by dividing inside the localization `B[1/b]` rather than by
a formula on representatives. The localization map `B ⟶ B[1/b]` is injective because `b` is a
nonzerodivisor, the evaluation `Stacks.Blowup.reesEval` is a ring map by construction, and so the
division map inherits the ring axioms from `Stacks.Blowup.reesEval` with no computation; this is
what `Stacks.Blowup.algebraMap_reesDivide` records. That the division is possible at all —
`Stacks.Blowup.reesAlgebra_le_reesDivisible` — is checked only on the degree-one generators
`monomial 1 x`, `x ∈ I`, by Mathlib's `adjoin_monomial_eq_reesAlgebra`.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. Tag 0806 is a statement about the blowup of an arbitrary
scheme in a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf, and asserts finality in the category `C`; what is proved
here is the existence of the classifying morphism for the *affine* blowup, under a hypothesis of
global (or local) principality that is strictly stronger than the effective Cartier condition of
`Stacks.Blowup.IsCartierOver`. Nothing here may be presented as a formalization of the tag.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0806](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0806)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01OG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 052Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/052Q)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry Polynomial

namespace Stacks.Blowup

universe u

section Ring

variable {R B : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing B] (φ : R →+* B) (I : Ideal R) (b : B)

/-- Evaluation of a polynomial at `1/b`, with coefficients carried along `φ`: the ring
homomorphism `R[X] ⟶ B[1/b]` sending `X` to the inverse of `b`. -/
def reesEval : R[X] →+* Localization.Away b :=
  eval₂RingHom ((algebraMap B (Localization.Away b)).comp φ) (IsLocalization.Away.invSelf b)

/-- The value of `monomial n x` at `1/b` is `φ x · b⁻ⁿ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem reesEval_monomial (n : ℕ) (x : R) :
    reesEval φ b (monomial n x) =
      algebraMap B (Localization.Away b) (φ x) * IsLocalization.Away.invSelf b ^ n := by
  simp [reesEval]

/-- The value of the constant polynomial `C x` at `1/b` is `φ x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem reesEval_C (x : R) :
    reesEval φ b (C x) = algebraMap B (Localization.Away b) (φ x) := by
  simp [reesEval]

/-- The polynomials whose value at `1/b` already lies in `B`. -/
def reesDivisible : Subalgebra R R[X] where
  carrier := {f | ∃ c : B, algebraMap B (Localization.Away b) c = reesEval φ b f}
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro f g ⟨c, hc⟩ ⟨d, hd⟩
    exact ⟨c * d, by rw [map_mul, hc, hd, map_mul]⟩
  add_mem' := by
    rintro f g ⟨c, hc⟩ ⟨d, hd⟩
    exact ⟨c + d, by rw [map_add, hc, hd, map_add]⟩
  algebraMap_mem' r := ⟨φ r, by simp⟩

/-- A polynomial lies in `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivisible φ b` if and only if its value at `1/b` is
the image of an element of `B`. -/
theorem mem_reesDivisible_iff {f : R[X]} :
    f ∈ reesDivisible φ b ↔ ∃ c : B, algebraMap B (Localization.Away b) c = reesEval φ b f :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- If `I` becomes the principal ideal `(b)` in `B`, then every element of the Rees algebra of
`I` has a value at `1/b` lying in `B`: the Rees algebra is generated over `R` by the monomials
`monomial 1 x` with `x ∈ I`, and such a monomial has value `c` where `φ x = c * b`. -/
theorem reesAlgebra_le_reesDivisible (hIb : I.map φ = Ideal.span {b}) :
    reesAlgebra I ≤ reesDivisible φ b := by
  rw [← adjoin_monomial_eq_reesAlgebra]
  refine Algebra.adjoin_le ?_
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  have hφx : φ x ∈ Ideal.span {b} := hIb ▸ Ideal.mem_map_of_mem φ hx
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp hφx
  refine ⟨c, ?_⟩
  rw [show ((monomial 1 : R →ₗ[R] R[X]) x) = monomial 1 x from rfl, reesEval_monomial, ← hc,
    map_mul, pow_one, mul_assoc, IsLocalization.Away.mul_invSelf, mul_one]

/-- Every element of the Rees algebra of `I` has a value at `1/b` lying in `B`, as soon as `I`
becomes the principal ideal `(b)` in `B`. -/
theorem exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval (hIb : I.map φ = Ideal.span {b}) (f : reesAlgebra I) :
    ∃ c : B, algebraMap B (Localization.Away b) c = reesEval φ b (f : R[X]) :=
  reesAlgebra_le_reesDivisible φ I b hIb f.2

/-- **Division by powers of `b`.** If `I` becomes the principal ideal `(b)` in `B` and `b` is a
nonzerodivisor, then the Rees algebra of `I` maps to `B`: a homogeneous element of degree `n`,
i.e. an element `x ∈ Iⁿ`, is sent to the unique `c ∈ B` with `φ x = bⁿ c`.

This is the ring map underlying the classifying morphism of Stacks tag 0806: it is the
degree-wise description of the graded algebra map `⨁ f^*ℐⁿ ⟶ ⨁ ℐ_Dⁿ` of the source's proof, in
the case where the inverse image divisor `D` is cut out by the single section `b`. -/
def reesDivide (hIb : I.map φ = Ideal.span {b}) (hb : b ∈ nonZeroDivisors B) :
    reesAlgebra I →+* B where
  toFun f := (exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval φ I b hIb f).choose
  map_one' := by
    apply Stacks.GradedRing.algebraMap_away_injective_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors b hb
    rw [(exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval φ I b hIb 1).choose_spec, map_one, OneMemClass.coe_one,
      map_one]
  map_mul' f g := by
    apply Stacks.GradedRing.algebraMap_away_injective_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors b hb
    rw [(exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval φ I b hIb (f * g)).choose_spec, map_mul,
      (exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval φ I b hIb f).choose_spec,
      (exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval φ I b hIb g).choose_spec, MulMemClass.coe_mul, map_mul]
  map_zero' := by
    apply Stacks.GradedRing.algebraMap_away_injective_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors b hb
    rw [(exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval φ I b hIb 0).choose_spec, map_zero, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero,
      map_zero]
  map_add' f g := by
    apply Stacks.GradedRing.algebraMap_away_injective_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors b hb
    rw [(exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval φ I b hIb (f + g)).choose_spec, map_add,
      (exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval φ I b hIb f).choose_spec,
      (exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval φ I b hIb g).choose_spec, AddMemClass.coe_add, map_add]

/-- The image of `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide φ I b hIb hb f` in `B[1/b]` is the value of `f` at
`1/b`. -/
@[simp]
theorem algebraMap_reesDivide (hIb : I.map φ = Ideal.span {b}) (hb : b ∈ nonZeroDivisors B)
    (f : reesAlgebra I) :
    algebraMap B (Localization.Away b) (reesDivide φ I b hIb hb f) = reesEval φ b (f : R[X]) :=
  (exists_algebraMap_eq_reesEval φ I b hIb f).choose_spec

/-- **The characterizing property of `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide`.** The image of a homogeneous
element of degree `n`, namely a monomial `monomial n x` with `x ∈ Iⁿ`, is the unique element of
`B` whose product with `bⁿ` is `φ x`. -/
theorem pow_mul_reesDivide_monomial (hIb : I.map φ = Ideal.span {b})
    (hb : b ∈ nonZeroDivisors B) {n : ℕ} {x : R} (hx : x ∈ I ^ n) :
    b ^ n * reesDivide φ I b hIb hb ⟨monomial n x, reesAlgebra.monomial_mem.mpr hx⟩ = φ x := by
  apply Stacks.GradedRing.algebraMap_away_injective_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors b hb
  rw [map_mul, map_pow, algebraMap_reesDivide, reesEval_monomial, mul_left_comm, ← mul_pow,
    IsLocalization.Away.mul_invSelf, one_pow, mul_one]

/-- `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide` is a map of `R`-algebras: in degree zero it is `φ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem reesDivide_algebraMap (hIb : I.map φ = Ideal.span {b}) (hb : b ∈ nonZeroDivisors B)
    (r : R) : reesDivide φ I b hIb hb (algebraMap R (reesAlgebra I) r) = φ r := by
  apply Stacks.GradedRing.algebraMap_away_injective_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors b hb
  rw [algebraMap_reesDivide, Subalgebra.coe_algebraMap]
  simp

/-- The degree-one element `monomial 1 x` of the Rees algebra of `I`, for `x ∈ I`. -/
def reesDegOne {x : R} (hx : x ∈ I) : reesAlgebra I :=
  ⟨monomial 1 x, reesAlgebra.monomial_mem.mpr (by simpa using hx)⟩

/-- `Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOne I hx` is homogeneous of degree one. -/
theorem reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading {x : R} (hx : x ∈ I) : reesDegOne I hx ∈ reesGrading I 1 :=
  (reesMonomial I 1 ⟨x, by simpa using hx⟩).2

/-- `x⁽¹⁾` is the monomial `x·T`. -/
theorem coe_reesDegOne {x : R} (hx : x ∈ I) :
    ((reesDegOne I hx : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) = monomial 1 x := rfl

/-- `Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide` divides the degree-one elements by `b`. -/
theorem mul_reesDivide_reesDegOne (hIb : I.map φ = Ideal.span {b})
    (hb : b ∈ nonZeroDivisors B) {x : R} (hx : x ∈ I) :
    b * reesDivide φ I b hIb hb (reesDegOne I hx) = φ x := by
  simpa [reesDegOne] using
    pow_mul_reesDivide_monomial φ I b hIb hb (n := 1) (by simpa using hx : x ∈ I ^ 1)

/-- **Maps out of the Rees algebra are determined in degrees zero and one**, because the Rees
algebra is generated over `R` by its degree-one part
(`Stacks.Blowup.adjoin_reesGrading_one_eq_top`). -/
theorem reesHom_ext {ψ χ : reesAlgebra I →+* B}
    (h0 : ∀ r : R, ψ (algebraMap R (reesAlgebra I) r) = χ (algebraMap R (reesAlgebra I) r))
    (h1 : ∀ y ∈ reesGrading I 1, ψ y = χ y) : ψ = χ := by
  let E : Subalgebra R (reesAlgebra I) := { ψ.eqLocus χ with algebraMap_mem' := h0 }
  have hE : (⊤ : Subalgebra R (reesAlgebra I)) ≤ E := by
    rw [← adjoin_reesGrading_one_eq_top]
    exact Algebra.adjoin_le h1
  exact RingHom.ext fun y => hE (Algebra.mem_top (R := R) (x := y))

/-- **`Stacks.Blowup.reesDivide` is the unique ring map out of the Rees algebra that extends `φ`
and divides the degree-one elements by `b`.** -/
theorem eq_reesDivide (hIb : I.map φ = Ideal.span {b}) (hb : b ∈ nonZeroDivisors B)
    (ψ : reesAlgebra I →+* B) (h0 : ∀ r : R, ψ (algebraMap R (reesAlgebra I) r) = φ r)
    (h1 : ∀ (x : R) (hx : x ∈ I), b * ψ (reesDegOne I hx) = φ x) :
    ψ = reesDivide φ I b hIb hb := by
  refine reesHom_ext I (fun r => by rw [h0, reesDivide_algebraMap]) fun y hy => ?_
  have hy1 : ((y : R[X])).coeff 1 ∈ I := by simpa using y.2 1
  rw [show y = reesDegOne I hy1 from Subtype.ext (coe_eq_monomial I hy)]
  refine sub_eq_zero.mp ((mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff.mp hb).1 _ ?_)
  rw [mul_sub, h1 _ hy1, mul_reesDivide_reesDegOne, sub_self]

/-- **The irrelevant ideal of the Rees algebra generates the unit ideal of `B`.** This is the
hypothesis under which `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.fromOfGlobalSections` produces a morphism into
`Proj` of the Rees algebra: the images of the degree-one elements `monomial 1 x`, `x ∈ I`,
already generate, because `b` lies in the ideal generated by the `φ x` and
`φ x = b · reesDivide _`. -/
theorem map_reesDivide_irrelevant_eq_top (hIb : I.map φ = Ideal.span {b})
    (hb : b ∈ nonZeroDivisors B) :
    (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (reesGrading I)).toIdeal.map (reesDivide φ I b hIb hb) = ⊤ := by
  set J := (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (reesGrading I)).toIdeal.map (reesDivide φ I b hIb hb)
  have hmem : I ≤ (Ideal.span {b} * J).comap φ := fun x hx =>
    Submodule.mem_span_singleton_mul.mpr
      ⟨reesDivide φ I b hIb hb (reesDegOne I hx),
        Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (HomogeneousIdeal.mem_irrelevant_of_mem (reesGrading I)
          Nat.one_pos (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hx)),
        mul_reesDivide_reesDegOne φ I b hIb hb hx⟩
  have hb' : b ∈ Ideal.span {b} * J :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr hmem (hIb ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self b)
  obtain ⟨y, hyJ, hy⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton_mul.mp hb'
  have hy1 : y = 1 := by
    refine sub_eq_zero.mp ((mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff.mp hb).2 (y - 1) ?_)
    rw [sub_mul, one_mul, mul_comm y b, hy, sub_self]
  exact Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ (hy1 ▸ hyJ) isUnit_one

end Ring

section Scheme

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) {X : Scheme.{u}} (φ : R →+* Γ(X, ⊤))
  (t : Γ(X, ⊤)) (hIt : I.map φ = Ideal.span {t}) (ht : t ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, ⊤))

/-- **The classifying morphism to the blowup.** -/
def toBlowUpSpec : X ⟶ blowUpSpec I :=
  Proj.fromOfGlobalSections (reesGrading I) (reesDivide φ I t hIt ht)
    (map_reesDivide_irrelevant_eq_top φ I t hIt ht)

/-- The composite `R ⟶ (reesGrading I) 0 ⟶ reesAlgebra I ⟶ Γ(X, ⊤)` is `φ`. -/
theorem reesDivide_comp_algebraMap_comp_reesGradingZeroEquiv :
    ((reesDivide φ I t hIt ht).comp
        (algebraMap (reesGrading I 0) (reesAlgebra I))).comp
      (reesGradingZeroEquiv I).toRingHom = φ := by
  refine RingHom.ext fun r => ?_
  show reesDivide φ I t hIt ht
      (algebraMap (reesGrading I 0) (reesAlgebra I) (algebraMap R (reesGrading I 0) r)) = φ r
  rw [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply, reesDivide_algebraMap]

/-- The classifying morphism `Stacks.Blowup.toBlowUpSpec` is a morphism over `Spec R`: its
composite with `Stacks.Blowup.toSpec I` is the structure morphism `X ⟶ Spec R` given by `φ`. -/
theorem toBlowUpSpec_toSpec :
    toBlowUpSpec I φ t hIt ht ≫ toSpec I = X.toSpecΓ ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom φ) := by
  show Proj.fromOfGlobalSections (reesGrading I) (reesDivide φ I t hIt ht)
        (map_reesDivide_irrelevant_eq_top φ I t hIt ht) ≫
      Proj.toSpecZero (reesGrading I) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (reesGradingZeroEquiv I).toRingHom) =
      X.toSpecΓ ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom φ)
  rw [Proj.fromOfGlobalSections_toSpecZero_assoc, ← Spec.map_comp, ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp,
    reesDivide_comp_algebraMap_comp_reesGradingZeroEquiv]

end Scheme

section Existence

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The ring map `R ⟶ Γ(X, ⊤)` corresponding to a morphism `X ⟶ Spec R`. -/
abbrev specHomRingHom (f : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of R)) : R →+* Γ(X, ⊤) :=
  CommRingCat.Hom.hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).inv ≫ f.appTop)

/-- A morphism `f : X ⟶ Spec R` is the composite of `X ⟶ Spec Γ(X, ⊤)` with the morphism
`Spec Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ Spec R` induced by `Stacks.Blowup.specHomRingHom f`. -/
theorem toSpecΓ_comp_specMap_specHomRingHom (f : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of R)) :
    X.toSpecΓ ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (specHomRingHom (R := R) f)) = f := by
  rw [CommRingCat.ofHom_hom, Spec.map_comp, ← Scheme.toSpecΓ_naturality_assoc,
    toSpecΓ_SpecMap_ΓSpecIso_inv, Category.comp_id]

/-- **The existence half of Stacks tag 0806 over an affine base, for a globally principal
inverse image of the centre.**

Let `X` be a scheme over `Spec R` and let `I ⊆ R` be an ideal. If the inverse image of `I` in
`Γ(X, ⊤)` is the principal ideal generated by a nonzerodivisor `t`, then `X` admits a morphism
to the blowup of `Spec R` in `I` over `Spec R`. -/
theorem exists_hom_toSpec (f : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of R)) (t : Γ(X, ⊤))
    (hIt : I.map (specHomRingHom (R := R) f) = Ideal.span {t})
    (ht : t ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, ⊤)) :
    ∃ g : X ⟶ blowUpSpec I, g ≫ toSpec I = f :=
  ⟨toBlowUpSpec I _ t hIt ht, by
    rw [toBlowUpSpec_toSpec, toSpecΓ_comp_specMap_specHomRingHom]⟩

/-- **The existence half of Stacks tag 0806 for a principal centre.** Every scheme over `Spec R`
on which the image of `a` is a nonzerodivisor admits a morphism over `Spec R` to the blowup of
`Spec R` in the principal ideal `(a)`.

This is the existence half of the universal property behind Stacks tag 0807 — blowing up an
effective Cartier divisor does nothing — in the affine case: an object of the category `C` of
tag 0806 for the centre `V(a)` is exactly a scheme over `Spec R` on which `a` becomes a
nonzerodivisor. -/
theorem exists_hom_toSpec_span_singleton (f : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of R)) (a : R)
    (ha : specHomRingHom (R := R) f a ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, ⊤)) :
    ∃ g : X ⟶ blowUpSpec (Ideal.span {a}), g ≫ toSpec (Ideal.span {a}) = f := by
  refine exists_hom_toSpec (Ideal.span {a}) f (specHomRingHom (R := R) f a) ?_ ha
  simp [Ideal.map_span]

end Existence

section Glue

variable {S S' T : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **Existence of a morphism over `S` is local on the source.** Let `b : S' ⟶ S` be separated
and an isomorphism over an open `V` of `S`, and let `f : T ⟶ S`. If the inverse image of `V` is
scheme-theoretically dense in every scheme mapping to `T` by an open immersion, then a family of
morphisms over `S` defined on an open cover of `T` glues: they agree on the overlaps by the
uniqueness half of Stacks tag 0806.

For the blowup this is what reduces the existence half of tag 0806 to a statement local on the
source: `V` is the complement of the centre, the density hypothesis is tag 07ZU applied to the
effective Cartier divisors cut out on the members of the cover, and separatedness is tag 01O2. -/
theorem exists_hom_of_isOpenCover (b : S' ⟶ S) [IsSeparated b] {V : S.Opens} [IsIso (b ∣_ V)]
    (f : T ⟶ S)
    (hdense : ∀ (W : Scheme.{u}) (p : W ⟶ T), IsOpenImmersion p →
      Scheme.Opens.IsSchemeTheoreticallyDense ((p ≫ f) ⁻¹ᵁ V))
    {s : Type*} (U : s → T.Opens) (hU : TopologicalSpace.IsOpenCover U)
    (hex : ∀ i, ∃ g : (U i).toScheme ⟶ S', g ≫ b = (U i).ι ≫ f) :
    ∃ g : T ⟶ S', g ≫ b = f := by
  choose g hg using hex
  have hcomp : ∀ i j : s, pullback.fst (U i).ι (U j).ι ≫ g i =
      pullback.snd (U i).ι (U j).ι ≫ g j := by
    intro i j
    refine eq_of_comp_eq b (f := (pullback.fst (U i).ι (U j).ι ≫ (U i).ι) ≫ f)
      (hdense _ _ inferInstance) _ _ ?_ ?_
    · simp only [Category.assoc]
      rw [hg i]
    · simp only [Category.assoc]
      rw [hg j, pullback.condition_assoc]
  refine ⟨(T.openCoverOfIsOpenCover U hU).glueMorphisms g hcomp, ?_⟩
  refine Scheme.Cover.hom_ext (T.openCoverOfIsOpenCover U hU) _ _ fun i => ?_
  exact (congrArg (· ≫ b)
    (Scheme.Cover.ι_glueMorphisms (T.openCoverOfIsOpenCover U hU) g hcomp i)).trans (hg i)

/-- **The existence half of Stacks tag 0806 over an affine base, from local data.**

Let `X` be a scheme over `Spec R` and `I ⊆ R` an ideal. Then `X` admits a morphism to the blowup
of `Spec R` in `I` over `Spec R` as soon as

* the blowup is an isomorphism over an open `V` of `Spec R` (tag 02OS part 1);
* the inverse image of `V` is scheme-theoretically dense in every open of `X` (tag 07ZU, applied
  to the effective Cartier divisor cut out on each open);
* on each member of some open cover of `X`, the inverse image of `I` is generated by a single
  nonzerodivisor.

Separatedness of the blowup of an affine scheme, the remaining input of
`Stacks.Blowup.exists_hom_of_isOpenCover`, is `Stacks.Blowup.instIsSeparatedToSpec`. -/
theorem exists_hom_toSpec_of_isOpenCover {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R)
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of R))
    {V : (Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).Opens} [IsIso (toSpec I ∣_ V)]
    (hdense : ∀ (W : Scheme.{u}) (p : W ⟶ X), IsOpenImmersion p →
      Scheme.Opens.IsSchemeTheoreticallyDense ((p ≫ f) ⁻¹ᵁ V))
    {s : Type*} (U : s → X.Opens) (hU : TopologicalSpace.IsOpenCover U)
    (hprincipal : ∀ i, ∃ t : Γ((U i).toScheme, ⊤),
      I.map (specHomRingHom ((U i).ι ≫ f)) = Ideal.span {t} ∧
        t ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ((U i).toScheme, ⊤)) :
    ∃ g : X ⟶ blowUpSpec I, g ≫ toSpec I = f := by
  refine exists_hom_of_isOpenCover (toSpec I) f hdense U hU fun i => ?_
  obtain ⟨t, hIt, htz⟩ := hprincipal i
  exact exists_hom_toSpec I ((U i).ι ≫ f) t hIt htz

end Glue

end Stacks.Blowup

